Subject: [PATCH 0/2] Archive from notmuch-emacs with the archive tag
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>

On this list "a" in notmuch-emacs should mean "archive this message".
Archiving for good is moving the file under maildir/archive/, which
"[PATCH v2] mail: Add just archive" [1] does for every message tagged
archive. These two patches make the key set that tag and keep the
message out of the inbox until the move.

Patch 1 sets notmuch-archive-tags to ("+archive" "-inbox"). Patch 2
makes mail-tag.sh drop inbox from messages tagged archive, so the next
notmuch new does not put them back. Without it the "-inbox" in patch 1
lasts only until notmuch new.

inbox already stays off sent and replied messages on trunk. Moved
messages lose it through "[PATCH v2 1/2] notmuch: Tag messages under
archive/ as archived" [2]. With this series inbox is exclusive with
sent, replied, archive and archived.

Both patches apply to trunk alone. Patch 2 adds a line right after
the +inbox rule, next to where [2] adds its archived rules, and patch 1
sits just above the hunk of "[PATCH] emacs: Match notmuch saved
searches to the list's tags" [3], so either may need a trivial rebase.

Tested with a scratch notmuch database: a message tagged archive
(with or without -inbox) stayed out of the inbox across a rerun of
mail-tag.sh. Untagged mail kept inbox, and replied and sent were
unchanged.

